2026-11-27T04:00:50.8027543Z # LexMachina
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8027683Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8027883Z LexMachina is a **query-specific visual legal-research system for Swiss law**.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8028122Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8028782Z A user asks a legal question. The product retrieves relevant case law, generates a sourced answer, independently searches for contrary/limiting/exception authorities, and displays the retrieved jurisprudence as an interactive map so minority lines and outliers are harder to miss.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8029994Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030073Z Current MVP flow:
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030176Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030241Z ```
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030381Z question
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030575Z   -> live OpenCaseLaw retrieval + deterministic dedupe
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8030894Z   -> query-conditioned clusters/map (rendered immediately)
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8031161Z   -> lazy evidence hydration
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8031373Z   -> source-constrained generative answer
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8031634Z   -> independent adversarial counter-authority pass
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8031923Z   -> patch answer/evidence/statuses without moving the map
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8032198Z   -> clickable decision/source inspection
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8032441Z ```
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8032555Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8033301Z The repository is operated by an autonomous OpenCode/Ox engineering factory. The factory optimizes for **minimal repository-owner attention** and aggressive reuse of the prior LexMachina research/codebase.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8034357Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8035019Z `main` is intentionally a lightweight control plane. Full historical artifacts remain on accepted `lab/*` and cycle branches; only compact accepted-state summaries are mirrored to `main`.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8035923Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8035927Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8036035Z ## Run the v45 query-map product
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8036227Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8036729Z The v45 MVP entry point is `product/query_app.py`; `product/server.py` is the preserved legacy 174k-map server, not the query-product hot path.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8037312Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8037658Z The normal path uses live OpenCaseLaw retrieval and the free/local generative provider abstraction:
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8038102Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8038198Z ```bash
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8038468Z pip install -r product/requirements-query.txt
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8038843Z python product/query_app.py --port 8787
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8039153Z ```
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8039277Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8040146Z Open `http://127.0.0.1:8787/`. The UI renders the retrieved map first, then lazily hydrates evidence and enriches that same map with the sourced answer and independent counter-authority audit.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8040918Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8042131Z A local OpenAI-compatible backend (Ollama / LM Studio / vLLM) can be used by setting `LEX_GENAUDIT_BACKEND=local`, `LEX_OPENAI_BASE_URL`, and optionally `LEX_OPENAI_MODEL`. If no generative provider succeeds, LEX keeps the map and sources and visibly falls back to the extractive answer instead of pretending the generative audit succeeded.
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8043449Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8043788Z For deterministic offline development/tests:
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8044029Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8044115Z ```bash
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8044383Z python product/query_app.py --fixture --port 8787
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8044779Z pytest -q product/tests/test_query_map_mvp.py
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8045094Z ```
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8045217Z 
2026-11-27T04:00:50.8045667Z The extractive TF-IDF answer is a degraded fallback only. Normal v45 behavior is the promoted `generative-audit` contract 2.2.
