2026-11-27T04:18:27.6065701Z """Progressive query execution: first-page map, then background expansion.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6066012Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6066151Z Why this module exists
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6066396Z ----------------------
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6066749Z The two-phase contract in ``pipeline.py`` was progressive in *name* only.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6067237Z ``run_query_initial`` still ran the **entire** multi-channel retrieval —
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6067922Z query variants, DE/FR/IT language pages, citation expansion and leading cases,
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6068654Z up to 40 upstream requests — before returning anything.  Measured live on
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6069203Z 2026-10-15 (run 38665681083, real OpenCaseLaw, ``product/query_app.py``):
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6069679Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6069936Z     GET /api/query/start   136.79 s  (upstream_retrieval_s 136.61, local_map_s 0.18)
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6070626Z     GET /api/query/enrich  150.70 s  (model 101.69, evidence hydration 49.00)
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6070957Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6071510Z The owner/jurist doing the comparative human gate therefore stares at an empty
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6072213Z page for ~2.3 minutes before the first point is drawn.  QUERY_MAP_MVP §9A asks
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6072799Z for the opposite: render the first results immediately and expand toward
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6073249Z 100-300 in the background.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6073427Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6073642Z This module adds the missing first stage without touching the accepted
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6074090Z ``ocl_adapter`` component:
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6074253Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6074567Z 1. ``run_query_first_page``  — one bounded search stage (single upstream page),
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6075102Z    then local geometry.  This is the first thing the browser draws.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6075761Z 2. ``expand_query_bundle``  — the full retrieval, merged into the *same* map.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6076088Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6076187Z Map stability contract
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6076434Z ----------------------
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6076832Z Refitting TF-IDF + SVD + KMeans on the larger candidate set would silently move
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6077429Z points the researcher already looked at.  Expansion therefore reconstructs the
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6078041Z fitted projection from the bundle that was actually shipped (texts -> vectorizer
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6078600Z /SVD -> shipped coordinates, cluster ids and labels) and projects the new
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6079168Z decisions into *that* space, attaching each to its nearest existing cluster.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6079898Z Already-rendered points keep their exact ``x``, ``y``, ``cluster_id`` and
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6080423Z ``is_outlier``; cluster labels are never re-invented.  The same
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6080942Z "enrichment must not move the map" rule that ``enrich_query_bundle`` enforces
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6081508Z for the answer stage is therefore also enforced across retrieval stages.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6081834Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6082005Z Everything reported here is measured and exported into
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6082505Z ``provenance.progressive`` so an auditor can recompute it.
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6082895Z """
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6083134Z from __future__ import annotations
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6083542Z 
2026-11-27T04:18:27.6083648Z import copy
