2026-11-27T04:19:05.1959274Z #: Cluster-label term means are rounded to this many decimals before ranking, and
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1959962Z #: only terms that actually occur in the cluster are eligible.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1960215Z #:
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1960557Z #: Audit advisory F2 of cycle 38779139471: the committed bundle's sha256 was not
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1961211Z #: reproducible outside the environment that generated it — the same 154 decision
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1961790Z #: rows produced two different label orders elsewhere.  Root cause, measured on
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1962361Z #: the claim bundle rather than assumed: for a cluster of 1-5 decisions only a
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1962958Z #: handful of the 5000-vocabulary terms have a non-zero mean, so the 4th/5th label
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1963512Z #: slots were filled from *thousands of exactly tied zero-mean terms*, i.e. from
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1963888Z #: ``argsort``'s internal ordering rather than from the data.  Eligibility
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1964229Z #: (mean > 0) makes those slots meaningful, and ranking the remainder by
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1964581Z #: ``(-round(mean, LABEL_MEAN_DECIMALS), term)`` makes the label a pure function
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1964869Z #: of the cluster's text.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965055Z LABEL_MEAN_DECIMALS = 9
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965231Z LABEL_TOP_K = 5
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965332Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965335Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965473Z def label_terms(mean, terms, top_k: int = LABEL_TOP_K) -> list[str]:
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965798Z     """The terms that explain one cluster, in a reproducible order.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1965994Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1966157Z     Shared by the initial fit (:func:`build_map`) and by the recompute-on-merge
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1966526Z     path (:func:`_cluster_label`), which previously ranked terms independently
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1966850Z     and could therefore disagree about the same cluster.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1967080Z     """
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1967252Z     mean = np.asarray(mean, dtype=float).ravel()
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1967642Z     order = sorted(
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1967836Z         (i for i in range(len(terms)) if mean[i] > 0.0),
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968156Z         key=lambda i: (-round(float(mean[i]), LABEL_MEAN_DECIMALS), str(terms[i])),
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968449Z     )
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968637Z     return [str(terms[i]) for i in order[:top_k]]
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968794Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968797Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1968995Z def _cluster_label(model: MapModel, members: list[dict], top_k: int = LABEL_TOP_K) -> str:
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1969612Z     """Top TF-IDF terms of a cluster's members, in the fitted vectorizer space.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1969845Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1970010Z     Recomputed from the merged membership whenever decisions are added: a label
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1970392Z     explains *why a group exists*, and more members are better evidence for it.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1970763Z     The cluster id stays the same, so nothing the researcher already read moves.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1970987Z 
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1971125Z     Only terms present in the cluster are eligible, and the order is
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1971547Z     ``(-round(mean, LABEL_MEAN_DECIMALS), term)`` — deterministic across
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1971901Z     environments.  Note the scope: that fixes the *label ordering*, which was
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1972276Z     the defect audit F2 of cycle 38779139471 found; it is not what makes the
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1972737Z     artifact reproducible.  Artifact identity is
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1976660Z     ``product/replay_bundle.py::content_sha256``, which since run 38789874982
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1977281Z     also excludes the machine's absolute cache root and is verified at two
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1977845Z     different checkout paths.  A cluster with fewer than ``top_k`` present terms
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1979082Z     is labelled with the terms it actually has rather than padded with absent
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1979714Z     ones.
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1979930Z     """
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1980190Z     if not members or model.vectorizer is None:
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1980541Z         return ""
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1980775Z     try:
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1981126Z         X = model.vectorizer.transform([_body(d)[:6000] for d in members])
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1981589Z         mean = np.asarray(X.mean(axis=0)).ravel()
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1982017Z         terms = [str(t) for t in model.vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()]
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1982469Z         return ", ".join(label_terms(mean, terms, top_k))
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1982954Z     except ValueError:  # empty vocabulary (e.g. every member is empty text)
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1983370Z         return ""
2026-11-27T04:19:05.1983502Z 
