2026-11-27T04:34:47.9747247Z === conftest ===
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9747520Z """Test isolation for the product test suite.
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9747782Z 
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9747895Z Why this file exists
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9748145Z --------------------
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9748461Z Cycle 38726191935 committed five pytest byproducts into
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9748794Z ``results/product/human_gate_sessions_simulated/``. The mechanism was a test
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9749188Z that ran ``human_gate_finalize.py`` without ``--out`` while the CLI's simulated
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9749827Z output directory resolved *inside the repository*; ``core-lane.yml`` then ran
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9750204Z ``git add -A`` and the scratch became a lane result.
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9750456Z 
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9750600Z The output directories are now overridable through the environment
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9751088Z (``LEX_HUMAN_GATE_OUT_DIR`` / ``LEX_HUMAN_GATE_SIMULATED_OUT_DIR``). This module
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9751863Z points them at a temp directory **at import time** — pytest imports conftest
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9752278Z before it imports any test module, so ``human_gate_finalize`` reads the
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9752758Z override while it is being imported, before any test can reach the CLI without
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9753275Z ``--out``. A unit run therefore cannot write into the repository's immutable
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9753655Z ``results/`` tree even if a future test forgets ``--out`` or the override.
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9753968Z 
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9754112Z Tests that want the real repository directories import them explicitly
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9754611Z (``CANONICAL_DIR_DEFAULT`` / ``SIMULATED_DIR_DEFAULT``), and the evidence scanner
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9754981Z always reads the repository paths.
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9755113Z 
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9755192Z Query runtime self-heal
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9755367Z -----------------------
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9755633Z The second job in this file is the pinned *query* runtime.  ``core-lane.yml``
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9756048Z never runs ``product/bootstrap_query_env.sh``, so on a fresh runner the suite
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9756573Z reaches ``product/query/**`` (numpy/sklearn) with nothing installed and dies
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9757011Z with ``ModuleNotFoundError`` before a single product claim is tested - measured
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9757414Z on run 40262401687, whose agent hit that import failure and exited 0 with an
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9757777Z unchanged tree after ~526 s, so the wrapper's delta guard rejected it
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9758134Z (``LEX_ZERO_DELTA_REPAIR``, exit 67; ``quantum_expired=false``; no work-quantum
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9758426Z expiry occurred; evidence:
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9758773Z ``results/product/orchestration/CYCLE_40263666190_lane_cycle_log_evidence.json``).
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9759524Z ``audit_readiness.py`` already bootstraps for the *dossier* invocation, but the
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9760141Z lane wrapper invokes pytest directly, so the harness - not each test - owns the
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9760659Z fix: pytest imports this conftest before any test module, and
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9761187Z ``query_env.ensure()`` runs the documented one-command bootstrap at most once
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9762893Z per process and never raises.  Set ``LEX_QUERY_ENV_NO_AUTOBOOTSTRAP=1`` to
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9763489Z observe an uninstalled environment (the fresh-runner ``-S`` probes do).
2026-11-27T04:34:47.9763929Z """
